---
// src/pages/privacy.astro
import LegalLayout from "@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { LEGAL } from "@/data/legal";
---

<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy">
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>{LEGAL.owner}</strong> ("we", "us"), trading as <strong>{LEGAL.brand}</strong>, collects, uses and protects your personal data when you visit <strong>{LEGAL.siteUrl}</strong> (the "Website"), buy from us, commission work or contact us.
    We handle personal data in line with the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023
    (NDPA) and, where it applies to you, other data protection laws such as the
    GDPR.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who is responsible for your data</h2>
  <p>
   <strong>{LEGAL.owner}</strong> is the data controller. You can reach us at <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.email}`}>{LEGAL.email}</a>
  </p>

  <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Orders and checkout:</strong> your name, email address, phone
      number, delivery and billing addresses, and what you ordered.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Payments:</strong> handled by {LEGAL.paymentProvider}. We receive
      confirmation of payment, but we do not see or store your full card details.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Enquiries and commissions:</strong> your name, email address,
      message, and any reference images or details you choose to send.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Newsletter:</strong> your email address, if you subscribe.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your cart:</strong> items you add to your cart are saved in your
      own browser (local storage) on your device. They are not sent to us until
      you check out.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical data:</strong> IP address, browser and device type, and
      pages visited, collected through server logs and {LEGAL.analytics}.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. How and why we use it</h2>
  <div class="mb-6 overflow-x-auto">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr class="border-b border-neutral-300">
          <th>Purpose</th>
          <th>Data</th>
          <th>Lawful basis</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Process, ship and support your orders</td>
          <td>Contact, delivery and order details</td>
          <td>Performing a contract with you</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Handle commission enquiries and requests</td>
          <td>Contact details, messages, references</td>
          <td>Steps at your request before a contract; contract</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Send the newsletter and updates</td>
          <td>Email address</td>
          <td>Your consent (withdraw any time)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Keep records and meet tax and legal duties</td>
          <td>Order and payment records</td>
          <td>Legal obligation</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Secure and improve the Website, prevent fraud</td>
          <td>Technical data</td>
          <td>Our legitimate interests</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>4. Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We do not sell your personal data. We share it only with providers that help us run the business, and only what they need:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>{LEGAL.paymentProvider}, to process payments;</li>
    <li>{LEGAL.courier}, and other couriers, to deliver your order;</li>
    <li>{LEGAL.emailProvider}, to send emails and the newsletter;</li>
    <li>{LEGAL.hostingProvider}, to host the Website;</li>
    <li>professional advisers, and authorities where the law requires it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Instagram:</strong> our Website can show recent posts from our
    Instagram account. When those images load, they come from Instagram's
    servers, so Instagram may receive your IP address and device information.
    Links to Instagram take you to a site governed by Instagram's own policies.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Cookies and local storage</h2>
  <p>
    We use your browser's local storage to remember your cart, which is
    essential for the shop to work. {LEGAL.analytics} may be used to understand
    how the Website is used; where it sets non-essential cookies, we will ask
    for your consent first. You can clear local storage and cookies at any time
    in your browser settings (this will empty your cart).
  </p>

  <h2>6. Transfers outside Nigeria</h2>
  <p>
    Some of the providers above process data outside Nigeria. When your data is
    transferred abroad, we take steps to make sure it remains protected in line
    with the NDPA, for example by using providers that offer appropriate
    safeguards.
  </p>

  <h2>7. How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Order and payment records: {LEGAL.retentionYears} years, for tax and accounting.</li>
    <li>Enquiries and commission messages: up to 12 months after the conversation ends, or longer if a commission is ongoing.</li>
    <li>Newsletter: until you unsubscribe.</li>
    <li>Technical logs: for a short period, as set by our hosting provider.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. How we protect it</h2>
  <p>
    We use reasonable technical and organisational measures, such as encrypted
    connections (HTTPS) and limited access, to protect your data. No online
    service is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security. If a
    breach affects your rights, we will notify you and the regulator where the
    law requires.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the NDPA, you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>be informed about how your data is used;</li>
    <li>access the personal data we hold about you;</li>
    <li>have inaccurate data corrected;</li>
    <li>ask us to delete your data, or restrict how we use it, in certain circumstances;</li>
    <li>object to processing, including for direct marketing;</li>
    <li>receive your data in a portable format;</li>
    <li>withdraw consent at any time (this does not affect past processing);</li>
    <li>not be subject to decisions based solely on automated processing that significantly affect you.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To use any of these rights, email <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.email}`}>{LEGAL.email}</a>.
    We may need to verify your identity first, and we will respond without
    undue delay, normally within 30 days. You can unsubscribe from the
    newsletter at any time using the link in any email.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are unhappy with how we handle your data, please contact us first. You
    also have the right to complain to the Nigeria Data Protection Commission
    (NDPC), or to your local data protection authority if you live elsewhere.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Children</h2>
  <p>
    The Website is not directed at children under 18, and we do not knowingly
    collect their personal data. If you believe a child has given us their
    information, please contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy as the Website or the law changes. The "Last
    updated" date at the top shows the latest version. If we make significant
    changes, we will take reasonable steps to let you know.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about privacy? Email <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.email}`}>{LEGAL.email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>